C++20 compound-requirement `{ E } -> C` evaluation ([expr.prim.req.compound]/1):
the return-type-requirement is checked as C<decltype((E))>.  Pre-increment of an
arithmetic lvalue yields an lvalue ([expr.pre.incr]/1), so decltype((++a)) is an
lvalue-reference and SameAs<decltype((++a)), int&> holds.  Guards both the
compound-requirement return-type evaluation and the C++ pre-increment/decrement
value-category fix.  See doc/architectural/cpp-requires-expression-support.md.

KNOWNBUG since round 152: main() was only partially type-checked and the
run reported SUCCESSFUL over the truncated body (user-reported Issue 13);
an incomplete user function is an error now.  Underlying failure: static assertion failed: ++int is int&

Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 (static assertion "++int is int&" failed): the
type-constraint's explicit argument `T &` -- a compound type naming the
enclosing parameter, not a bare cpp_name -- was passed to the synthetic
concept-id unsubstituted and unresolved.  Fixed 2026-09-23: such an
argument is substituted through the enclosing map and type-checked before
the concept-id is evaluated.
